    <section class="hu-read-section" id="start">
      <p class="hu-read-p">On October 12 I sat down with Device Assembly on my phone and couldn't plug a hose into an
      outlet. Every check we had said the game worked on a phone. Every button on the page passed the 44 pixel touch rule,
      and that was true. The wall itself, where you actually play, was 28 percent of an iPhone SE's screen with squares 11
      pixels wide, and nothing was measuring in there.</p>
      <p class="hu-read-p">Post 1 drew the line for 1.0 at the October 11 review. I thought the week after it would be
      cleanup. It turned into two new daily puzzles and a pile of fixes to the way we check things.</p>
    </section>

